<%- include('../partials/header') %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Download your data</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    Everything this parish has entered, in a form you can keep, print, or move
    to another system. The records are yours. This page is how you get a copy
    of them without asking anyone.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="stats" style="margin-bottom:22px">
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= stats.families %></div><div class="k">Families</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= stats.members %></div><div class="k">People</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= photos %></div><div class="k">Photographs</div></div>
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="n"><%= stats.families - stats.published %></div>
    <div class="k">Drafts, not printed</div>
  </div>
</div>

<form method="get" action="<%= base %>/admin/export.zip" class="card" id="download-form">
  <h2>What to include</h2>

  <div class="field">
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" name="drafts" value="0" id="skip-drafts">
      Leave out drafts &mdash; only the
      <strong><%= stats.published %></strong> entries that go into the printed book
    </label>
    <p class="help">
      Drafts are included by default. Leave them in for a copy you are keeping;
      take them out for a copy you are handing to a printer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="submit" class="btn">Spreadsheet and photographs (.zip)</button>
    <button type="submit" class="btn ghost" formaction="<%= base %>/admin/export.csv">
      Spreadsheet only (.csv)
    </button>
    <button type="submit" class="btn ghost"
            formaction="<%= base %>/admin/export-photos.zip"
            <%= photos ? '' : 'disabled' %>>
      Photographs only (.zip)
    </button>
  </div>

  <p class="help">
    The full archive holds <code>families.csv</code> and a <code>photos</code>
    folder. Each photograph is named after the family it belongs to. The last
    column of the spreadsheet gives that same name, so you can match a row to
    a face without opening the app.
  </p>

  <p class="help">
    <% if (photos) { %>
      <strong>Photographs only</strong> gives you just the pictures, each file
      named for its <strong>Family ID</strong> alone, like
      <code>F-001.jpg</code>. That is exactly what
      <a href="<%= base %>/admin/photos">Import photographs</a> reads back. So
      you can take the folder out, replace the pictures that are wrong, and
      upload the same folder again without renaming a single file.
    <% } else { %>
      <strong>Photographs only</strong> is not available yet because no family
      in this parish has a photograph. Add them from each family&rsquo;s own
      page, or a folder at a time on
      <a href="<%= base %>/admin/photos">Import photographs</a>.
    <% } %>
  </p>
</form>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Before you send it anywhere</h2>
  <p class="help" style="margin-top:0">
    This file holds every address, phone number and date of birth in the
    parish, along with the photographs. It has no password. Treat it the way
    the parish would treat the printed directory before it is handed out, and
    delete the copy in your downloads folder once it has reached wherever it
    was going.
  </p>
  <p class="help">
    The spreadsheet has one row per person, with the family&rsquo;s details
    repeated on each of their rows. That is the shape Excel can sort and
    filter. A file with one row per family cannot hold all the members.
  </p>
  <p class="help">
    A download of a few thousand photographs takes minutes and runs to
    hundreds of megabytes. It starts right away, and nothing is stored on the
    server while it runs. If the browser looks idle, it is still working, so
    do not click again &mdash; that starts a second download.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
